---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---

<ToolLayout
  slug="markdown-preview"
  title="Markdown Preview"
  description="Live editor with split-pane preview, GFM support, and HTML sanitization. Real-time stats and copy-to-clipboard functionality."
  heading="Markdown Editor & Preview"
  intro="Write markdown on the left, see a live preview on the right. Supports GitHub Flavored Markdown with tables, task lists, and strikethrough — all output is sanitised before display."
>
  <div slot="input" class="md-editor-wrapper">
    <div class="md-split">
      <div class="md-pane md-input-pane">
        <label class="md-label mono">Markdown input</label>
        <textarea
          id="md-input"
          class="md-textarea"
          spellcheck="false"
          placeholder="# Hello&#10;&#10;Try writing some **markdown** here. Tables, code blocks, and strikethrough all work.&#10;&#10;- [ ] Task list&#10;- [x] With checkboxes&#10;&#10;```js&#10;const x = 42;&#10;```"
        ></textarea>
        <div class="md-stats">
          <div class="md-stat">
            <span class="md-stat-label">Words</span>
            <span class="md-stat-value" id="md-words">0</span>
          </div>
          <div class="md-stat">
            <span class="md-stat-label">Characters</span>
            <span class="md-stat-value" id="md-chars">0</span>
          </div>
          <div class="md-stat">
            <span class="md-stat-label">Read time</span>
            <span class="md-stat-value" id="md-readtime">—</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="md-pane md-preview-pane">
        <div class="md-label mono">Preview (sanitised)</div>
        <div id="md-preview" class="md-preview"></div>
        <p class="md-sanitise-note mono">Output is sanitised with DOMPurify</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="md-actions">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="md-copy-html">Copy HTML</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="md-copy-source">Copy source</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="md-clear">Clear</button>
    </div>

    <p class="md-feedback" id="md-feedback" role="alert"></p>
  </div>

  <section class="section md-notes-sec">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="glass-card md-note-card">
        <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="code" /></span>
        <div>
          <h2 class="h3">What is GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM)?</h2>
          <p>
            CommonMark is the baseline: standard markdown with headings, lists, bold, italic, links, images,
            code blocks, and blockquotes. GitHub Flavored Markdown extends it with three powerful additions:
          </p>
          <ul class="md-note-list">
            <li><b>Tables</b> — organize data in rows and columns</li>
            <li><b>Task lists</b> — checkboxes for to-do items and progress tracking</li>
            <li><b>Strikethrough</b> — mark text as deleted or superseded</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            This tool renders GFM, so all three features work here. But GFM is GitHub's extension, not a
            universal standard — if you move markdown to another platform, these features may not render
            the same way.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="glass-card md-note-card">
        <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="shield" /></span>
        <div>
          <h2 class="h3">Why is HTML sanitisation important?</h2>
          <p>
            When you convert markdown to HTML, the output is just text — until a browser renders it. Raw HTML
            can contain scripts, event handlers, and other code that runs when the page loads. This is an
            XSS (cross-site scripting) vulnerability if the markdown input is not fully trusted.
          </p>
          <p>
            This tool uses <b>DOMPurify</b> to strip any dangerous elements before display. Unsafe tags,
            attributes, and event handlers are removed. The preview you see is safe to read, and the HTML
            you copy is safe to paste. However, sanitisation also removes some legitimate formatting — for
            example, inline styles are stripped for safety.
          </p>
          <p class="md-note-limit">
            <b>For trusted content:</b> If you control the markdown source (you wrote it, or it came from your
            own system), sanitisation is extra caution. <b>For untrusted content:</b> (pasted from the
            internet, user-generated) sanitisation is essential — never render untrusted HTML without it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ToolLayout>

<style>
  .md-editor-wrapper { margin-top: 26px; }

  .md-split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    min-height: 500px;
  }

  .md-pane {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .md-label {
    font-size: 0.6rem !important;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding: 14px 16px 0;
  }

  .md-input-pane { position: relative; }

  .md-textarea {
    flex: 1;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    resize: none;
    word-break: break-word;
    outline: none;
  }

  .md-textarea::placeholder { color: var(--text-muted); }

  .md-stats {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 12px 16px 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .md-stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }

  .md-stat-label { color: var(--text-muted); }

  .md-stat-value {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .md-preview-pane {
    position: relative;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    overflow-y: auto;
  }

  .md-preview {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* ---- markdown element styles ---- */
  .md-preview :global(h1),
  .md-preview :global(h2),
  .md-preview :global(h3),
  .md-preview :global(h4),
  .md-preview :global(h5),
  .md-preview :global(h6) {
    margin: 24px 0 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .md-preview :global(h1) { font-size: 1.8rem; margin-top: 0; }
  .md-preview :global(h2) { font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .md-preview :global(h3) { font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .md-preview :global(h4) { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .md-preview :global(h5),
  .md-preview :global(h6) { font-size: 1rem; }

  .md-preview :global(p) { margin: 0 0 12px; }

  .md-preview :global(ul),
  .md-preview :global(ol) {
    margin: 12px 0;
    padding-left: 2em;
  }

  .md-preview :global(li) { margin-bottom: 6px; }

  .md-preview :global(blockquote) {
    margin: 12px 0;
    padding-left: 14px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--border-strong);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .md-preview :global(code:not(pre code)) {
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    background: var(--surface-strong);
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  .md-preview :global(pre) {
    margin: 12px 0;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    background: var(--term-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--term-border);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .md-preview :global(pre code) {
    color: var(--term-text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .md-preview :global(table) {
    margin: 12px 0;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .md-preview :global(th) {
    padding: 8px 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface-strong);
    color: var(--text-soft);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .md-preview :global(td) {
    padding: 8px 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .md-preview :global(tr:nth-child(even)) { background: var(--surface); }

  .md-preview :global(input[type="checkbox"]) {
    margin-right: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .md-preview :global(del) { color: var(--text-muted); text-decoration: line-through; }

  .md-preview :global(strong) { font-weight: 600; }

  .md-preview :global(em) { font-style: italic; }

  .md-preview :global(a) {
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .md-preview :global(a:hover) { color: var(--accent-cyan); }

  .md-preview :global(img) {
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .md-preview :global(hr) {
    margin: 18px 0;
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .md-sanitise-note {
    font-size: 0.6rem !important;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .md-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .md-feedback {
    min-height: 20px;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .md-feedback.is-error { color: var(--accent-red); }

  .md-notes-sec { padding-block: clamp(30px, 4vw, 56px); background: var(--bg-elev); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }

  .md-note-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 46px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .md-note-card:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .md-note-card h2 { margin-bottom: 10px; }

  .md-note-card p { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; }

  .md-note-card p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .md-note-card b { color: var(--text-soft); font-weight: 600; }

  .md-note-list {
    margin: 10px 0 10px 1.5em;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: disc;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .md-note-list li { margin-bottom: 4px; }

  .md-note-limit { padding-top: 12px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .md-split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; min-height: 400px; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .md-note-card { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .md-actions { flex-direction: column; }
    .md-actions .btn { width: 100%; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);

  const input = $('md-input') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
  const preview = $('md-preview');
  const feedback = $('md-feedback');
  const wordCount = $('md-words');
  const charCount = $('md-chars');
  const readTime = $('md-readtime');

  let lastMarkdown = '';

  const esc = (s) => String(s ?? '').replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;');

  function updateStats(text) {
    const chars = text.length;
    const words = text.trim().split(/\s+/).filter((w) => w.length > 0).length;
    const readMinutes = Math.ceil(words / 200);

    if (charCount) charCount.textContent = chars.toString();
    if (wordCount) wordCount.textContent = words.toString();
    if (readTime) readTime.textContent = readMinutes < 1 ? '< 1 min' : `${readMinutes} min`;
  }

  async function renderMarkdown(text) {
    if (text === lastMarkdown) return;
    lastMarkdown = text;

    if (!text.trim()) {
      if (preview) preview.innerHTML = '';
      updateStats('');
      return;
    }

    try {
      // Dynamically import marked and dompurify only when needed
      const { marked } = await import('marked');
      const DOMPurify = await import('dompurify').then((m) => m.default);

      // Configure marked for GFM
      marked.setOptions({
        breaks: true,
        gfm: true,
      });

      // Render markdown to HTML
      const html = await marked.parse(text);

      // Sanitize with DOMPurify
      const sanitised = DOMPurify.sanitize(html, {
        ALLOWED_TAGS: [
          'h1', 'h2', 'h3', 'h4', 'h5', 'h6',
          'p', 'br', 'hr',
          'strong', 'em', 'b', 'i', 'u', 'del', 's', 'sub', 'sup',
          'ul', 'ol', 'li',
          'blockquote',
          'pre', 'code',
          'table', 'thead', 'tbody', 'tr', 'th', 'td',
          'a',
          'img',
          'input',
        ],
        ALLOWED_ATTR: ['href', 'title', 'target', 'src', 'alt', 'type', 'checked', 'disabled'],
      });

      if (preview) preview.innerHTML = sanitised;
      updateStats(text);

      // Clear feedback on success
      if (feedback) {
        feedback.textContent = '';
        feedback.classList.remove('is-error');
      }
    } catch (err) {
      if (feedback) {
        feedback.classList.add('is-error');
        feedback.textContent = `Rendering error: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Unknown error'}`;
      }
    }
  }

  // Live preview on input
  input?.addEventListener('input', () => {
    renderMarkdown(input.value);
  });

  // Copy HTML button
  $('md-copy-html')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    if (!preview || !preview.innerHTML) {
      if (feedback) feedback.textContent = 'Nothing to copy — preview is empty.';
      return;
    }

    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(preview.innerHTML);
      if (feedback) {
        feedback.classList.remove('is-error');
        feedback.textContent = 'HTML copied to clipboard.';
      }
      setTimeout(() => {
        if (feedback) feedback.textContent = '';
      }, 2000);
    } catch {
      if (feedback) {
        feedback.classList.add('is-error');
        feedback.textContent = 'Failed to copy — clipboard access denied.';
      }
    }
  });

  // Copy source (markdown) button
  $('md-copy-source')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    if (!input.value) {
      if (feedback) feedback.textContent = 'Nothing to copy — editor is empty.';
      return;
    }

    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(input.value);
      if (feedback) {
        feedback.classList.remove('is-error');
        feedback.textContent = 'Markdown source copied to clipboard.';
      }
      setTimeout(() => {
        if (feedback) feedback.textContent = '';
      }, 2000);
    } catch {
      if (feedback) {
        feedback.classList.add('is-error');
        feedback.textContent = 'Failed to copy — clipboard access denied.';
      }
    }
  });

  // Clear button
  $('md-clear')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    input.value = '';
    renderMarkdown('');
    if (feedback) {
      feedback.textContent = '';
      feedback.classList.remove('is-error');
    }
  });

  // Load sample on page load
  function loadSample() {
    const sample = `# Markdown Preview

This is a live markdown editor with **GitHub Flavored Markdown** support.

## Features

- Split-pane editor and preview
- Real-time rendering and stats
- Sanitised output for security
- Support for tables, task lists, and more

## Code Example

\`\`\`javascript
const greet = (name) => {
  console.log(\`Hello, \${name}!\`);
};

greet('Lex Corp');
\`\`\`

## Task List

- [x] Write a markdown editor
- [x] Add live preview
- [ ] Deploy to production

## Table

| Feature | Status | Notes |
|---------|--------|-------|
| GFM tables | ✓ | Fully supported |
| Strikethrough | ✓ | Use ~~deleted~~ text |
| Task lists | ✓ | Checkboxes work |

## Blockquote

> Security matters. Always sanitise untrusted HTML before displaying it.

Visit [Lex Corp](https://www.lexcorp.com.np) for more.`;
    input.value = sample;
    renderMarkdown(sample);
  }

  // Load sample only if input is empty on first load
  if (!input.value) {
    loadSample();
  } else {
    renderMarkdown(input.value);
  }
</script>
